Improved: Portable::internal::resolve_hanging_nodes(), which resolves the
hanging-node constraints in Portable::FEEvaluation, now uses one thread per
constrained line of degrees of freedom instead of one per degree of
freedom. It needs no per-thread temporary array of the size of a cell and a
single team barrier per direction, which considerably speeds up matrix-free
operators on meshes with hanging nodes, in particular in 3d and for higher
polynomial degrees.
<br>
(Ivan Prusak, 2026/11/16)
